<title>SOUTH AFRICA: RUGBY UNION-NEW ZEALAND BEAT SOUTH AFRICA 35-32.</title>
<headline>RUGBY UNION-NEW ZEALAND BEAT SOUTH AFRICA 35-32.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-07-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>New Zealand beat South Africa 35-32 (halftime 19-23) in a Tri-Nations match at Ellis Park on Saturday.</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>New Zealand - Tries: Frank Bunce (2), Jeff Wilson, Carlos Spencer. Conversions: Carlos Spencer (3). Penalties: Spencer (3)</p>
<p>South Africa - Tries: Naka Drotske, Russell Bennett. Conversions: Jannie de Beer (2). Penalties: De Beer (4). Drop goal: De Beer (2).</p>
